005200231110:EHELP.
005300231110.*--------------------------------------------------------------------
005400231110.* Hilfetext für den Befehl
005500231110.*--------------------------------------------------------------------
005600231110:HELP NAME='CRTMSGDS'.
005700231110Create Message Data Structure (CRTMSGDS) - Help
005800231110:P.
005900231110The CRTMSGDS command is used to create a data structure for the
006000231110data fields of a message description. Also it is used to create a CL
006100231110program or a CL script for a message description. The CL script
006200231110then can be execute with the RUNCLSTM command in order to reproduce
006300231110the message description.
006400231110.*
006500231110:EHELP.
006600231110.*
006700231110.*--------------------------------------------------------------------
006800231110.* Hilfetext für Schlüsselwort RANGE
006900231110.*--------------------------------------------------------------------
007000231110:HELP name='CRTMSGDS/RANGE     '.
007100231110Range of message identifiers - Help
007200231110:XH3.Range of message identifiers (RANGE)
007300231110:P.
007400231110Specifies the range of message identifiers in the
007500231110specified message file which are processed by the command. All
007600231110message descriptions in the message file specified on the
007700231110:HP2.Message:EHP2. file prompt (MSGF parameter) can be processed
007800231110by specifying *ALL on this parameter.
007900231110:P.
008000231110If the starting message identifier is not specified, the
008100231110message descriptions begin with the first message in the
008200231110specified message file.  If the ending message identifier
008300231110is not specified, the default value, *ONLY, is used, and
008400231110only the description of the starting message identifier is
008500231110processed.
008600231110.*
008700231110:IMHELP name='COM/OPTPARM'.
008800231110.*
008900231110:XH3.Starting Message Identifier
009000231110:P.
009100231110The first of the two values in this parameter, called the
009200231110starting message identifier, specifies the message
009300231110identifier of the first message description to be processed.
009400231110:P.
009500231110:PARML.
009600231110:PT.:PK DEF.*FIRST:EPK.
009700231110:PD.The first message in the file specified on the :HP2.Message
009800231110file:EHP2. prompt (MSGF parameter) is the first message
009900231110whose description is processed.
010000231110:PT.:PV.lower-value:EPV.
010100231110:PD.Specify the 7-character identifier of the first
010200231110message description to be processed.
010300231110:EPARML.
010400231110:P.
010500231110:XH3.Ending Message Identifier
010600231110:P.
010700231110The second of the two values, called the ending message
010800231110identifier, specifies the message identifier for the last
010900231110message description to be processed.
011000231110:P.
011100231110:PARML.
011200231110:PT.:PK DEF.*ONLY:EPK.
011300231110:PD.Only the message identifier specified as a starting
011400231110message identifier is processed.
011500231110:PT.:PV.*LAST:EPV.
011600231110:PD.The last message in the file is the last message whose
011700231110description is processed.
011800231110:PT.:PV.upper-value:EPV.
011900231110:PD.Specify the 7-character identifier of the last message
012000231110description to be processed.
012100231110:EPARML.
012200231110:P.
012300231110:XH3.Other Single Values:
012400231110:P.
012500231110:PARML.
012600231110:PT.:PV.*ALL:EPV.
012700231110:PD.All message descriptions in the message file specified
012800231110are processed.  This value can only be specified in the first
012900231110element of this parameter.
013000231110:EPARML.
013100231110.*
013200231110:EHELP.
013300231110.*
013400231110.*--------------------------------------------------------------------
013500231110.* Hilfetext für Schlüsselwort MSGF
013600231110.*--------------------------------------------------------------------
013700231110:HELP name='CRTMSGDS/MSGF'.
013800231110Message file - Help
013900231110:XH3.Message file (MSGF)
014000231110:P.
014100231110Specifies the name and library of the message file from
014200231110which the message descriptions are taken.
014300231110.*
014400231110:IMHELP name='COM/OPTPARM'.
014500231110.*
014600231110:PARML.
014700231110:PT.:PK DEF.QCPFMSG:EPK.
014800231110:PD.Message descriptions are taken from the system message
014900231110file, QCPFMSG.
015000231110:PT.:PV.message-file-name:EPV.
015100231110:PD.Specify the name of the message file from which the
015200231110message descriptions are taken.
015300231110:EPARML.
015400231110:P.
015500231110The possible library values are:
015600231110:P.
015700231110:PARML.
015800231110:PT.:PK DEF.*LIBL:EPK.
015900231110:PD.All libraries in the job's library list are searched
016000231110until the first match is found.
016100231110:PT.:PV.*CURLIB:EPV.
016200231110:PD.The current library for the job is used to locate the
016300231110message file.  If no current library entry exists in
016400231110the library list, QGPL is used.
016500231110:PT.:PV.library-name:EPV.
016600231110:PD.Specify the library where the message file is located.
016700231110:EPARML.
016800231110.*
016900231110:EHELP.
017000231110.*
017100231110.*--------------------------------------------------------------------
017200231110.* Hilfetext für Schlüsselwort FILE
017300231110.*--------------------------------------------------------------------
017400231110:HELP name='CRTMSGDS/FILE'.
017500231110File - Help
017600231110:XH3.File (FILE)
017700231110:P.
017800231110Specifies the name and library of the source file that contains the
017900231110source member or where the member is added.
018000231110.*
018100231110:IMHELP name='COM/OPTPARM'.
018200231110.*
018300231110:PARML.
018400231110:PT.:PK DEF.QCOPYLE:EPK.
018500231110:PD.The source member is added to the QCOPYLE source file.
018600231110:PT.:PV.source-file-name:EPV.
018700231110:PD.Specify the name of the source file that the member
018800231110is added to.
018900231110:EPARML.
019000231110:P.
019100231110The possible library values are:
019200231110:P.
019300231110:PARML.
019400231110:PT.:PK DEF.*LIBL:EPK.
019500231110:PD.All libraries in the job's library list are searched
019600231110until the first match is found.
019700231110:PT.:PV.*CURLIB:EPV.
019800231110:PD.The current library for the job is used to locate the
019900231110message file.  If no current library entry exists in
020000231110the library list, QGPL is used.
020100231110:PT.:PV.library-name:EPV.
020200231110:PD.Specify the library where the message file is located.
020300231110:EPARML.
020400231110.*
020500231110:EHELP.
020600231110.*
020700231110.*--------------------------------------------------------------------
020800231110.* Hilfetext für Schlüsselwort MBR
020900231110.*--------------------------------------------------------------------
021000231110:HELP name='CRTMSGDS/MBR'.
021100231110Member - Help
021200231110:XH3.Member (MBR)
021300231110:P.
021400231110Specifies the name of the source member that is used to take the output of
021500231110the CRTMSGDS command. If *GEN is specified, then a separate member name
021600231110is produced for each message description. If a member name is specified, then
021700231110the output of all message description specified is directed to that member.
021800231110.*
021900231110:IMHELP name='COM/OPTPARM'.
022000231110.*
022100231110:PARML.
022200231110:PT.:PK DEF.*GEN:EPK.
022300231110:PD.The name of the source member is produced based on the message identifier.
022400231110:PT.:PV.source-member-name:EPV.
022500231110:PD.Specify the name of the source member that is taken to get the output
022600231110of the CRTMSGDS command.
022700231110:EPARML.
022800231110.*
022900231110:EHELP.
023000231110.*
023100231110.*--------------------------------------------------------------------
023200231110.* Hilfetext für Schlüsselwort REPLACE
023300231110.*--------------------------------------------------------------------
023400231110:HELP name='CRTMSGDS/REPLACE'.
023500231110Replace member - Help
023600231110:XH3.Replace member (REPLACE)
023700231110:P.
023800231110Specifies whether an existing member is allowed to be replaced
023900231110or not.
024000231110.*
024100231110:IMHELP name='COM/OPTPARM'.
024200231110.*
024300231110:PARML.
024400231110:PT.:PK DEF.*NO:EPK.
024500231110:PD.An existing member is not replaced. An error message is issued
024600231110by the command instead.
024700231110:PT.:PV.*YES:EPV.
024800231110:PD.The content of an existing member is replaced.
024900231110:EPARML.
025000231110.*
025100231110:EHELP.
025200231110.*
025300231110.*--------------------------------------------------------------------
025400231110.* Hilfetext für Schlüsselwort TYPE
025500231110.*--------------------------------------------------------------------
025600231110:HELP name='CRTMSGDS/TYPE'.
025700231110Source type - Help
025800231110:XH3.Source type (TYPE)
025900231110:P.
026000231110Specifies the type of source that is produced by the CRTMSGDS command.
026100231110.*
026200231110:IMHELP name='COM/OPTPARM'.
026300231110.*
026400231110:PARML.
026500231110:PT.:PK DEF.*ILERPG:EPK.
026600231110:PD.An ILE-RPG data structure is produced.
026700231110:PT.:PV.*RPG:EPV.
026800231110:PD.A RPG-III data structure is produced.
026900231110:PT.:PV.*C:EPV.
027000231110:PD.A C data structure is produced.
027100231110:PT.:PV.*CLP:EPV.
027200231110:PD.A CL program is produced.
027300231110:PT.:PV.*CLLE:EPV.
027400231110:PD.An ILE CL program is produced.
027500231110:PT.:PV.*SCRIPT:EPV.
027600231110:PD.A CL script is produced.
027700231110:EPARML.
027800231110.*
027900231110:EHELP.
028000231110.*
028100231110.*--------------------------------------------------------------------
028200231110.* Hilfetext für Schlüsselwort DEFINE
028300231110.*--------------------------------------------------------------------
028400231110:HELP name='CRTMSGDS/DEFINE'.
028500231110Create DEFINE specifications - Help
028600231110:XH3.Create DEFINE specifications (DEFINE)
028700231110:P.
028800231110Specifies whether DEFINE specification are added to the source member
028900231110or not. The value for this parameter can only be specified if
029000231110:HP2.Source type:EHP2. (parameter TYPE) is set to *ILERPG or *C.
029100231110.*
029200231110:IMHELP name='COM/OPTPARM'.
029300231110.*
029400231110:PARML.
029500231110:PT.:PK DEF.*YES:EPK.
029600231110:PD.DEFINE specification are added to the source member.
029700231110:PT.:PV.*NO:EPV.
029800231110:PD.DEFINE specification are not added to the source member.
029900231110:EPARML.
030000231110.*
030100231110:EHELP.
030200231110.*
